{
  "_name": "s33_mixed_cr_channel_overhear",
  "_desc": "Mixed-CR CHANNEL OVERHEAR (2026-07-27). s32's dual-CR gateway topology plus channel posts originated BY the gateways, so an M_BROADCAST/FLOOD is transmitted on a cr8 layer while the overhearing leaves sit at the global cr5. Exists to make the two OVERHEAR-RETUNE sites validatable: node_mac_rx.cpp:154 (FLOOD) and :185 (M_BROADCAST) size the overhearer's retune window with active_cr() -- the OVERHEARER's own CR -- not the sender's, the same defect class as start_pending_rx_expiry fixed by \u00a7rts-cr. The RTS-M already carries the sender's CR (cr_adv), so the fix is one token per site; before this scenario existed there was no way to prove it.",
